# Drafted by Gemini (R24 king), edited.

~ arrive
cutscene ct_six_horns_his_crown
Narrator: You step into a wide glade of grey grass where a barren, twisted oak knots its own bare limbs forty feet overhead.
cutscene ct_six_horns_his_crown_2
Narrator: Above those tangled boughs, the Crooked Moon hangs terribly close and bright, her carved crone's face grinning down at the mound.
cutscene end
set ct_clearing_entered
-> END

~ tree
Narrator: Up on its stony mound, the ancient oak smells of cold sap and old iron, with a great bleached goat skull resting among its roots.
* Look at the bark -> tree_face
* Look at the skull -> tree_skull
* Leave -> END

~ tree_face
Narrator: The ridges of the dark bark shift with a dry creak, shaping the high cheekbones and lidded eyes of a watching queen.
-> tree

~ tree_skull
Narrator: Between the sweeping horns of the skull hangs a little wooden crescent moon on twine, bone and carving alike bitter cold to the touch.
-> tree

~ emerge
if flag.ct_all_bargained
-> kneel_offer
endif
-> fight

~ kneel_offer
Narrator: Thirty feet of black fur, leathery wing, and six-horned crown blot out the stars, waiting in the quiet grass as the last of you climbs up.
ct_hk_goat [smile]: Each of you took my hand in the dark. Why raise cold iron now, when a place at the Queen's right hand awaits you?
* Fight him anyway -> fight
* Kneel -> kneel_1

~ kneel_1
ct_hk_goat [sly]: Be sure of your heart, little lambs. When she rises, the Hollow and every straight thing in it will be unmade and bent anew.
* Yes, we kneel -> kneel_2
* No, we fight -> fight

~ kneel_2
Narrator: The pines around the glade lock their branches tight, and the great beast's three red eyes burn warm against the frost.
ct_hk_goat [neutral]: Once the knee bends, everything that was is ended. Do you give the world to the root and the briar?
* Yes. We kneel. -> kneel_done
* No. We fight. -> fight

~ kneel_done
Narrator: You sink into the cold grass, and the roots rise gentle around your shoulders to grant every wish you asked for, crooked and eternal.
ct_hk_goat [smile]: Rise, then, children of the bough. Your heart's desire is yours, crooked and whole, for all the endless night.
set ct_kneeled
quest the_horned_kings_offer kneeled
quest the_crooked_tree crooked_rebirth
end_game
-> END

~ fight
set crooked_cause = "wipe"
cutscene ct_born_king
Narrator: The great beast spreads its bat wings and bares a dragon's furnace maw, six horns scraping the silver light.
cutscene ct_born_king_2
Narrator: High in the trunk of the Crooked Tree, the fey queen's wooden face splits open in a silent, splintering laugh.
cutscene end
quest the_crooked_tree born_king
combat ct_born_king

~ tree_burnt
Narrator: The Crooked Tree burns without smoke, a tall clean flame the colour of an old lamp, and the moon above it has stopped grinning.
Narrator: Embers lift off the branches in the thousands and go up into the dark, and where they pass, the grass is already starting to grow green.
-> END
